In summary:

  ADDED, wholly new work by Oliver D'Souza — the Lean library ZetaQ/ (33 modules), its root module
  ZetaQ.lean and ZetaQ/README.md; the scripts and receipt files under audit/; the ZetaQ entries in
  lakefile.toml; and, inside Zeta23/, the three modules Zeta23/WindowD.lean,
  Zeta23/Tail/GevreyTail.lean and Zeta23/Taper/GevreyProduct.lean, with the two corresponding
  imports added to Zeta23.lean. Each of these files carries its own copyright header naming
  Oliver D'Souza, including the three added modules under Zeta23/ -- which do not exist upstream,
  and whose headers were corrected accordingly: two had inherited the upstream Anthropic header by
  copy from neighbouring files, and one carried no header at all.
  ZetaQ/ imports Zeta23 and is not part of the upstream artifact: it is a separate development in
  the conductor aspect, it is not sorry-free, and it is deliberately outside lakefile.toml's
  defaultTargets, so that `lake build` still builds only the upstream library.

  CHANGED, inside the upstream Zeta23/ — Zeta23/Defs.lean gains the weakened standing-assumption
  class Params.ValidQ (Params.Valid with the bandwidth cap lam_le_one dropped) and the implication
  Valid.validQ; and twenty-one further modules under Zeta23/ have hypotheses of the form
  (hP : P.Valid) replaced by (hP : P.ValidQ), with the corresponding call sites adapted by inserting
  .validQ. These are hypothesis WEAKENINGS: every affected statement is generalised, no conclusion
  is altered, and no declaration is removed or renamed. No other change was made under Zeta23/.

  ADDED for the follow-up of October 2026, wholly new work by Oliver D'Souza — the Lean libraries
  ZetaS/ (the zeta follow-up; imports Zeta23), ZetaSCertShims/ (bare-name forwarders for the
  certificate checker in ZetaS/Cert/), ZetaShell/ (the family follow-up; imports ZetaQ) and
  ZetaSReplay/ (1,478 generated modules: the kernel replay of the K = 5 certificate), with their
  root modules ZetaS.lean and ZetaShell.lean and their entries in lakefile.toml; under comparator/,
  the topic FollowUpZeta (ChallengeDeps/FollowUpZeta.lean, Challenge/FollowUpZeta.lean,
  Solution/FollowUpZeta.lean, PrintAxioms/FollowUpZeta.lean, config-followup.json,
  README_followup.md), the topic FollowUpFamily (the four files FollowUpFamily.lean in the same
  folders, config-followup-family.json and README_followup_family.md) and the files
  PrintAxioms/FollowUpShell.lean and PrintAxioms/FollowUpReplay.lean; supplementary/ (certificate data, certifier scripts, logs and the
  replay generator); papers/; audit/followup/; CITATION.cff, .zenodo.json and RELEASE_NOTES.md; and
  entries in .gitattributes and .gitignore. All of it is Copyright 2026 Oliver D'Souza and licensed
